@base = http://localhost:5118
@alice = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@bob = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### Each request becomes ONE message for ONE actor (account/1111…)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}

### The actors in memory: Alice and Bob, activated by their opening at startup
GET {{base}}/system

### Withdrawal refused: a business refusal is a normal response (400), not a failure
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 5000 }

### ─── Concurrency without locks ───

### 1,000 withdrawals of 3 € fired AT THE SAME TIME on Alice's account: exactly 333 accepted, final balance 1 €, never negative
POST {{base}}/demo/simultaneous-withdrawals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "account": "{{alice}}", "count": 1000, "amount": 3 }

### 500 transfers Alice → Bob and 500 Bob → Alice at the same time: no deadlock, total preserved
POST {{base}}/demo/crossed-transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "count": 500, "amount": 1 }

### ─── Let it crash: failures and supervision ───

### Trap Alice's account: its next withdrawal will crash AFTER changing the balance in memory, BEFORE writing it
POST {{base}}/system/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actor": "account/{{alice}}", "step": "BeforeSave" }

### → 500: the actor crashed, its supervisor replaced it with a fresh incarnation
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 1 }

### The withdrawal did not happen: the new incarnation read the storage again (the balance did not move)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}

### The supervisor's log
GET {{base}}/system/log

### Trap Bob's account 4 times: 3 restarts per minute, then stop (quarantine)
POST {{base}}/system/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actor": "account/{{bob}}", "step": "Reception", "times": 4 }

### Run 5 times: 500, 500, 500, 500, then 503 until the end of the minute (Alice, however, still answers)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{bob}}

### A slowness of 8 s: the request answers 504 after 5 s; the message, however, will be processed
POST {{base}}/system/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actor": "account/{{alice}}", "step": "Reception", "kind": "Slowness", "latencyMs": 8000 }

###
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}

### ─── Transfers: one actor per transfer ───

### A transfer identified by the client (replayable without risk)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "invoice-42", "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 10 }

### Replayed: same response, no new debit (the actor transfer/invoice-42 remembers)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "invoice-42", "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 10 }

### Failure in the middle of a transfer, after the debit: 500, the money is "in flight"…
POST {{base}}/system/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actor": "transfer/invoice-43", "step": "AfterDebit" }

###
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "invoice-43", "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 10 }

### … status DebitDone
GET {{base}}/transfers/invoice-43

### … replaying completes it, without debiting a second time
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "invoice-43", "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 10 }

### To an account that does not exist: debit, refusal from the target, compensation (status Cancelled)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999", "amount": 10 }

### ─── Activation and passivation ───

### Put all the idle actors to sleep (automatic after 30 s without a message)
POST {{base}}/system/passivation

### No actor left in memory…
GET {{base}}/system

### … but their state is still stored
GET {{base}}/system/storage?type=account

### The next message wakes up Alice, and her alone
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/operations
